      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Update:\n\nGetting the same error again now.\n\ntried around again with more things.\n\ncurrently it seems VRChat starts the first time after PC boot, but then either after a VRChat crash or when i closed it, it does not start up again without closing itself.\n\nStill no out of the ordinary log entry (except that it just stops)\n\nwindows events log only shows EAC loading and unloading.\n\nI am really out of options what could cause this. Starting VRChat.exe directly, it does not close after a couple seconds and shows the \"You are in offline testing mode\" message.\n\nStarting launch.exe again closes it after 1-5 seconds.\n\nsome new things i tried:\n\n- disabling CPU cores.\n\n- uninstalled Bitdefender (because of mention of https://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/video-players-crash-game-bitdefender)\n\n- enabling the DPI-scaling overwriting (because i read somewhere it could help when using high-dpi second screens)\n\nbut all still no avail.\n\nWindows 11 is still relatively fresh installed. I know people say VRChat is not Windows 11 compatible. But why would it then sometimes run, then sometimes not. And sometimes even no issue for weeks.\n\n(however i don't know if i might just have got lucky for weeks and having to only start VRChat a single time. Who knows. will keep an eye on that.)\n\nIf it would just provide any hint about any error. Just closing is not helpful.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-02-06T00:58:46.757Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Today i started having the issue that VRChat just closes itself after around 5 seconds.\n\nI see the login screen, i was once even quick enough to login with my login credentials, but then it just closed itself while loading the world.\n\nI installed Windows 11 yesterday, but also played for some time with windows 11, so i think its not really an issue with windows 11, but i barely changed anything else. (mostly just windows update, driver update).\n\nAnd now when i start VRChat, i can see the login screen for 3 to 5 seconds and then the window just goes away. Steam mostly thinks VRChat is still running for some more time.\n\nI tried uninstalling, reinstalling, moved VRChat to a different drive, tried everything described here:\n\nhttps://help.vrchat.com/hc/en-us/articles/1500002247921-VRChat-keeps-crashing-or-has-issues-launching-properly\n\nbut it still does not work.",
